\section*{Introduction}
Visual Question Answering (VQA) involves answering questions about images, a task that has recently gained significant attention. Conversely, Visual Question Generation (VQG) seeks to create questions from images. While VQG has been explored in prior research, it has not been as extensively studied as VQA. In this paper, we propose a new VQG framework that utilizes a large collection of images to generate a diverse range of questions. Our method is trained on a dataset of 1.2 million image-question-answer triples, where each image is associated with 1,,000 questions. We show that this method can effectively enhance VQG performance by producing more diverse questions. Our approach is simple yet effective, and we demonstrate that it can be integrated with existing VQG models to improve performance. The code and data are available at https://github.com/rohitgarg1/VQG-Diverse.

